      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Pennsylvania Route 272, called Nottingham Road, cuts through the community, linking it 23 miles to Lancaster and 6 miles to Nottingham.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Britain%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community drains west to Little Conowingo Creek and south via Reynolds Run to Octoraro Creek, both feeding the Susquehanna River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Little_Britain%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Daniel F. Magee detailed Little Britain Township’s early settlement, including Fulton Township, in a 1913 journal article.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://lancasterhistory.org/images/stories/JournalArticles/vol17no5pp138_151_362579.pdf",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1913 Journal of the Lancaster County Historical Society published Magee’s account of Little Britain’s early settlement.",
